WEBVTT

00:00:00.285 --> 00:00:02.355
An outbound request missed its mock.

00:00:02.526 --> 00:00:06.466
Start with that one call and find out what
the responder used to match it.

00:00:07.019 --> 00:00:10.244
Open the replay report and select Mocked
Responses.

00:00:10.415 --> 00:00:14.280
Filter by Match Status, choose No Match,
and open one request.

00:00:14.451 --> 00:00:16.417
Stay on the endpoint you want to fix.

00:00:16.985 --> 00:00:20.201
Open Signature and inspect the keys used
for matching.

00:00:20.372 --> 00:00:24.675
Compare the incoming request with a
candidate from Suggested Signatures.

00:00:24.846 --> 00:00:28.747
A differing value can explain why the
recorded response was skipped.

00:00:29.285 --> 00:00:33.841
If you've confirmed a key changes between
runs and does not select a different

00:00:33.841 --> 00:00:35.477
response, queue its removal.

00:00:35.647 --> 00:00:38.809
Keep the HTTP method and endpoint filters.

00:00:38.979 --> 00:00:42.312
For a database lookup, keep the keys that
select the row.

00:00:42.852 --> 00:00:47.474
Open Pending Transform Changes and check
the key, method, and endpoint.

00:00:47.645 --> 00:00:50.134
Apply the change and create a new report.

00:00:50.305 --> 00:00:54.050
Keeping the change small makes it easier to
tell what fixed the miss.

00:00:54.619 --> 00:00:59.550
Go back to Mocked Responses, find the same
request pattern, and check that it now

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.411
shows Match and returned the expected
response.

00:01:02.582 --> 00:01:06.095
Use the overall mock accuracy metric as a
second check.

00:01:06.652 --> 00:01:11.083
If the mock responds with the wrong data,
put the key back and narrow the change.
